<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/64801AJPTMMJGDJQHDKQNBCGKMVGLSGLB>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "CRFF Blue Heron";
  schema:description """
	Within a re-creation of childhood joys lies a more troubling story of a family’s growing crisis in Sophy Romvari’s affecting and intelligent feature debut. The graceful opening scenes depict a period of transition for a Hungarian Canadian family of six as they adapt to a new home on Vancouver Island in the late 1990s, seen from the perspective of the youngest daughter Sasha. Fascinating and moving as a meditation on grief, memory, and love, Blue Heron sees the filmmaker blur the borders between fiction and documentary in ways that aren’t soon forgotten.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>90 minutes<span><br/></span>Not Rated<span><br/></span>Content Advisory: Mature themes<span><br/></span>English, Hungarian<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $20 Admission (+applicable taxes & fees)
""";
