<http://www.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/event/63001AJJHHCCDTKKSDNHNCJHVRPDPDKLT>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Tentacle Tribe";
  schema:description """
	Returning to Campbell River, Tentacle Tribe transcends the boundaries between street and contemporary dance with a striking piece - ‘DIRT’ - for five virtuoso performers.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Through its raw expression, this creation is a critique of humanity’s conquering relationship with the planet. The quintet mixes puppets and movements in an unusual conceptual hip-hop. Choreographed by Elon Höglund, this work is a profound meditation on our ancestral connection with the Earth.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Artichaut Mag, Mathilde Côté:</span><span class=\"ItalicText\"> “This breathtaking performance, blending street and contemporary dance, is a cry from the heart — a breath of (dis)hope nestled in the cracks of a crumbling world.”</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">La Presse, Iris Gagnon-Paradis:</span> “Dirt, the new creation by Tentacle Tribe, is a work brimming with ingenious ideas and a particularly refined aesthetic.”<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">“…he (Höglund) thus succeeds in creating something that feels truly new, exciting, and above all, meaningful — notably by incorporating a more organic physicality inspired by the animal world.”</span><span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Tentacle Tribe</span> is a Montreal-based dance company co-founded in 2012 by Canadian dancer Emmanuelle Lê Phan and Swedish dancer Elon Höglund. Approaching choreography through a wide variety of movement philosophies, Tentacle Tribe concocts uncommon dance works with a contemporary approach.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The company is internationally renowned for its unique style of \"conceptual hip-hop,\" blending b-boying, b-girling, and street dance with contemporary flow. Tentacle Tribe has toured nationally and globally across contemporary and street dance festivals and presentations. www.tentacletribe.com/the-company<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"BoldText\">Please visit BC Movement Arts Society</span> for more information and for our Tentacle Tribe shows in Sointula. <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.bcmovementarts.com\">www.bcmovementarts.com</a><span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Tickets: $38.00 Adult, $35.00 Senior, $33.00 Student, $13.00 Child under 5, $31.00 Groups 10+ <span class=\"ItalicText\">(+applicable taxes & fees)</span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-10-15T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/tidemarktheatre/files/b3011b53-fd50-41d5-ac2b-9f5e7b7edcfc.jpg>;
